{
 "ambiguities": [
  {
   "choice": "Round 3 / round 1: 'Counted only from the shadow restart ... (start record code_sha = that merge commit)'. Chosen: the LAST start record at or after T0 is the run origin (stricter: a later restart resets the 24 h); all start t_ms and code_sha are reported; n_starts_after_t0 > 1 blocks tool_rules_clear. A rerun with --since-ms at the later start is a new clock and needs its own clean-checkout record. The origin's code_sha must equal --expect-code-sha (change 1).",
   "id": "A01",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "Which start record, when more than one has t_ms >= T0"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Item 1 uses covered_h: window_end = min(--until-ms, largest used t_ms); a hole is any interval longer than 600,000 ms between consecutive points of [origin, hb t_ms..., window_end]; covered_h = (window_end - origin - sum(holes)) / 3,600,000. elapsed_h, covered_h, hb_max_gap_ms and n_holes are printed.",
   "id": "A02",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "Elapsed and covered hours (replaced by change 10)"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Item 2: 'on at least 90% of trigger records'. Chosen: pv and fv triggers; both the share over ALL triggers and the share over no-gap pv triggers with ws >= 1 must reach 90% (stricter). 'ok' needs status == 'ok' AND a non-null integer value. A known share below 90% is a fail even if the other share is null; null only when no known share fails and one is unknown (change 7).",
   "id": "A03",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "'trigger records' in the 90% coverage (item 2)"
  },
  {
   "choice": "'gap false' is read as gap is exactly False; a missing or null gap is not no-gap.",
   "id": "A04",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "no-gap"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Item 2: 'base_union.status ok on at least 90%'. Chosen: status == 'ok' and the union value base_breaks_unresolved_settled_union a non-null integer.",
   "id": "A05",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "Union ok (item 2)"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Round 3 (R2 C7 f): would-pass is pv-only, by construction (would_pass_n == would_pass_pv_n). A fv trigger that passes everything else is counted separately as fv_not_eligible_variant_n ('not eligible: variant'). The executor acts on pv only. The pv plus fv sum is never called trades.",
   "id": "A06",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "Would-pass variants"
  },
  {
   "choice": "boost_src must be one of 'pda', 'event_authority'. 'none' (no BOOST identity known, so dropped_boost_n is 0 by construction), 'behavioural', any other string and a missing key fail C3. would_pass_by_boost_src stays reported.",
   "id": "A07",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "C3 boost_src (R1, round 3)"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Not decidable from records. The start record 'rule' ids are reported; C6 is NOT applied and is listed as outside_tool_pending.",
   "id": "A08",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "C6 'v1 only'"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Reported three ways: sequential funnel C1..C4, C5a, C5b, C5c; leave-one-out (passes all others, fails this one); and for C5 parts among C1-C4 triggers: failing the part at all, failing only that part, failing all three, failing any.",
   "id": "A09",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "'removes' per C condition (item 6)"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Share of ws-0 no-gap plain pool closes with tipauth >= 1 OR orphaned_by_drop_n >= 1, over closes with base_tipauth.status ok and a non-null value (n_ok). met is null when n_ok < 100 (INCOMPLETE_MIN_OK), else share_of_ok <= 5%. Both shares stay reported.",
   "id": "A10",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "Tip incompleteness share (item 5) (replaced by change 2)"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Every unsealed trigger and pool record that carries a base_tipauth dict. 'a base_tipauth without the dropped key' is counted literally (an exception record counts here and in union_errors). A malformed dropped entry (not [str, None-or-int, int slot]) is counted as its own violation. A missing trigger slot or margin_slots when the trigger bound must be checked is a violation. union_errors = largest hb counters.union_errors in the run; an hb whose counters dict lacks the key is a 0-valued sample, an hb whose value is present but not an integer counts as 1 (fail closed). A trigger or pool record whose pool is not a string is left out of every count and counted in record_pool_not_str (must be 0).",
   "id": "A11",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "Consistency checks apply to"
  },
  {
   "choice": "Also applied to an empty list: dropped_first_slot / dropped_last_slot must then be null (status ok).",
   "id": "A12",
   "status": "RULED",
   "topic": "'dropped_n <= 20 with last entry slot != dropped_last_slot'"
  },
  {
   "choice": "'Tested' = entries classified still dropped or left D. Undetermined entries are reported and excluded from the denominator. The close used is the FIRST close of the pool with t_ms >= the trigger's; if it is not status ok with integer cover_hi >= the trigger slot, all that trigger's entries are undetermined (no skipping ahead). Distinct entries are keyed (pool, signature, event_index) (class: left D if any row is, else still dropped if any, else undetermined). fire(t, l) = (l >= 1) if t < 100 else (l / t > 0.01); met is false if fire on the per-row counts or on the distinct counts.",
